From 8928e2b1e84d05247c40149548e077afe3473587 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:17:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 80/98] pvr: keep up to 16 render target datasets for reuse

Four were too few for frames with many renders of several sizes, each
kept by the command buffers of the frames in flight: glmark2's desktop
scenes still created and destroyed a free list and RT dataset (plus
their buffer objects) for most renders. A dataset for a window-sized
render is a few small buffers.

glmark2-es2 through zink, off-screen 800x600, FPS of two runs each,
before -> after: desktop blur 51/51 -> 62/62, desktop shadow 144/139 ->
152/157, the others unchanged.

CTS: as for the previous commit, identical to before.
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_rt_dataset.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_rt_dataset.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_rt_dataset.c
index b827903..bd45675 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_rt_dataset.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_rt_dataset.c
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ void pvr_rt_vheap_rtc_data_fini(struct pvr_rt_dataset *rt_dataset)
 }
 
 /* Datasets kept for reuse; each holds a few BOs sized by the render area. */
-#define PVR_RT_CACHE_MAX 4
+#define PVR_RT_CACHE_MAX 16
 
 static void pvr_rt_dataset_free(struct pvr_rt_dataset *rt_dataset)
 {
-- 
2.47.3

